di, vendredi et samedi: de 11:00 \u00e0 18:00"],"nl":["maandag en zondag: gesloten","dinsdag, woensdag, donderdag, vrijdag en zaterdag: van 11:00 tot 18:00"],"en":["monday and sunday: closed","tuesday, wednesday, thursday, friday and saturday: from 11:00 to 18:00"],"de":["monday and sunday: closed","tuesday, wednesday, thursday, friday and saturday: from 11:00 to 18:00"],"it":["monday and sunday: closed","tuesday, wednesday, thursday, friday and saturday: from 11:00 to 18:00"],"sp":["monday and sunday: closed","tuesday, wednesday, thursday, friday and saturday: from 11:00 to 18:00"],"pt":["monday and sunday: closed","tuesday, wednesday, thursday, friday and saturday: from 11:00 to 18:00"],"cn":["monday and sunday: closed","tuesday, wednesday, thursday, friday and saturday: from 11:00 to 18:00"]},"date_start":"2023-01-12","date_end":"2023-03-04","is_also_by_appointment":false}],"prices":[],"child_events":[],"parent_events":[],"targets":{"list":[],"translations":{}},"opening":{"day":"2023-01-12","start":"18:00:00","timestamp":"2023-01-12T18:00:00+01:00","end":"21:00:00","is_only_by_appointment":false},"tags":[],"accessibilities":[],"facebook_link":null,"publication_state":"public","last_updated_at":"2023-02-12T03:35:10+01:00","published_at":"2022-12-05T15:48:10+01:00","backoffice_id":266684,"import_origin":null,"sub_type":"expo","show_in_agenda":true,"ranking":0.33755319058958},{"id":548517,"date_start":"2023-01-12","date_end":"2023-03-04","date_next":"2023-02-14","accept_article27":false,"accept_cultuurbon":false,"accept_paspartoe":false,"is_closed_on_public_holidays":true,"is_closed_on_school_holidays":false,"is_only_by_appointment":false,"is_permanent":false,"is_free":false,"is_online":false,"is_canceled":false,"is_soldout":false,"categories":{"main":{"id":23,"translations":{"fr":"Exposition","nl":"Tentoonstellingen","en":"Exhibition","de":"Ausstellung","it":"Esposizioni","sp":"Exhibici\u00f3n","pt":null,"cn":null}},"others":{"list":[24,26],"translations":{"fr":["Galeries d'art","Sculpture"],"nl":["Galeries","Beeldhouwkunst"],"en":["Art Galleries","Sculpture"],"de":["Kunstgalerien","Skulptur"],"it":["Gallerie d'arte","Scultura"],"sp":["Galer\u00edas de arte","Escultura"],"pt":[null,null],"cn":[null,null]}}},"languages":{"spoken":["fr","en","nl"],"subtitles":[]},"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Marcin Sobolev - 'Central Asia'","shortdescr":"La galerie Baronian, en collaboration avec Cedric Emelinckx, est heureuse d'annoncer Central Asia, la premi\u00e8re exposition personnelle de Marcin Sobolev \u00e0 la galerie.","longdescr":"La galerie Baronian, en collaboration avec Cedric Emelinckx, est heureuse d'annoncer Central Asia, la premi\u00e8re exposition personnelle de Marcin Sobolev \u00e0 la galerie. Les \u0153uvres couvrent un r\u00e9cit personnel, d\u00e9peignant de mani\u00e8re abstraite des extraits et des sc\u00e8nes de la vie quotidienne dans les villes du Caucase et des r\u00e9gions recul\u00e9es d'Asie centrale.\r\nEntre les influences de la musique locale, de l'art populaire, de la culture chamanique, du pass\u00e9 culturel et personnel, Sobolev d\u00e9veloppe son propre langage visuel qui, dans ses sculptures tot\u00e9miques et ses peintures d\u00e9taill\u00e9es, traduit sans effort l'\u00e9nergie des lieux visit\u00e9s. L'interaction de l'image et des \u0153uvres typographiques, du symbole et du contexte, du d\u00e9tail et de l'abstraction c\u00e9l\u00e8bre l'esth\u00e9tique vibrante de la vie quotidienne en Europe orientale urbaine et en Asie centrale rurale et met en avant ce qui est souvent cach\u00e9 : une cr\u00e9ativit\u00e9 impulsive qui produit un art honn\u00eate et pur. Les \u0153uvres de Sobolev sont un hommage au talent du peuple, \u00e0 un milieu qui oppose avec succ\u00e8s l'h\u00e9t\u00e9ronomie socio-\u00e9conomique \u00e0 sa propre volont\u00e9 cr\u00e9atrice. Il s'approprie le langage, le symbolisme et les r\u00e8gles, les ali\u00e8ne et les remplit de sa propre signification \u00e0 plusieurs niveaux, qui devient tangible dans la composition des \u0153uvres.","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.baronian.eu","email":"info@baronian.eu","phone_contact":"+32 2 512 92 95","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/fr\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.548517"},"nl":{"name":"Marcin Sobolev - 'Central Asia'","shortdescr":"Galerie Baronian, in samenwerking met Cedric Emelinckx, is verheugd Central Asia aan te kondigen, de eerste solotentoonstelling van Marcin Sobolev in de galerie.","longdescr":"Galerie Baronian, in samenwerking met Cedric Emelinckx, is verheugd Central Asia aan te kondigen, de eerste solotentoonstelling van Marcin Sobolev in de galerie. De werken bevatten een persoonlijk verhaal, waarin op abstracte wijze fragmenten en sc\u00e8nes uit het dagelijks leven in de steden van de Kaukasus en de afgelegen regio's van Centraal-Azi\u00eb worden weergegeven.\r\nTussen de invloeden van lokale muziek, volkskunst, sjamanistische cultuur, cultureel en persoonlijk verleden, ontwikkelt Sobolev zijn eigen beeldtaal die in zijn totemische sculpturen en gedetailleerde schilderijen moeiteloos de energie van de bezochte plaatsen overbrengt. Het samenspel van beeld en typografische werken, symbool en context, detail en abstractie viert de levendige esthetiek van het dagelijks leven in stedelijk Oost-Europa en landelijk Centraal-Azi\u00eb en brengt naar voren wat vaak verborgen is: een impulsieve creativiteit die eerlijke en pure kunst voortbrengt. Sobolevs werken zijn een eerbetoon aan het talent van de mensen, aan een milieu dat zich met succes verzet tegen sociaal-economische heteronomie met zijn eigen creatieve wil. Hij eigent zich taal, symboliek en regels toe, vervreemdt ze en vult ze met zijn eigen meerlagige betekenis, die tastbaar wordt in de compositie van de werken.","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.baronian.eu","email":"info@baronian.eu","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/nl\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.548517"},"en":{"name":"Marcin Sobolev - 'Central Asia'","shortdescr":"Marcin Sobolev, Belgian artist, presents his solo exhibition \u201cCentral Asia\u201d. The works cover a personal narrative, depicting in an abstract way excerpts and scenes of everyday life in the cities of the Caucasus and the remote regions of Central Asia.","longdescr":"Gallery Baronian, in collaboration with Cedric Emelinckx, is pleased to announce Central Asia, Marcin Sobolev\u2019s first solo exhibition at the gallery. The works cover a personal narrative, depicting in an abstract way excerpts and scenes of everyday life in the cities of the Caucasus and the remote regions of Central Asia.\r\nBetween the influences of local music, folk art, shamanic culture, cultural and personal past, Sobolev develops his own visual language which, in his totemic sculptures and detailed paintings, effortlessly conveys the energy of the places visited. The interplay of image and typographic works, symbol and context, detail and abstraction celebrates the vibrant aesthetics of everyday life in urban Eastern Europe and rural Central Asia and brings forward what is often hidden: an impulsive creativity that produces honest and pure art. Sobolev\u2019s works are a tribute to the talent of the people, to a milieu that successfully opposes socio-economic heteronomy with its own creative will. He appropriates language, symbolism and rules, alienates them and fills them with his own multi-layered meaning, which becomes tangible in the composition of the works.","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.baronian.eu","email":"info@baronian.eu","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/en\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.548517"},"de":{"name":"Marcin Sobolev - Central Asia","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.baronian.eu","email":"info@baronian.eu","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/de\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.548517"},"it":{"name":"Marcin Sobolev - Central Asia","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.baronian.eu","email":"info@baronian.eu","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/it\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.548517"},"sp":{"name":"Marcin Sobolev - Central Asia","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.baronian.eu","email":"info@baronian.eu","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/sp\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.548517"},"pt":{"name":"Marcin Sobolev - Central Asia","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.baronian.eu","email":"info@baronian.eu","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/pt\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.548517"},"cn":{"name":"Marcin Sobolev - Central Asia","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.baronian.eu","email":"info@baronian.eu","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/cn\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.548517"}},"place":{"id":238078,"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Baronian","address_street_name":"Rue Isidore Verheyden","address_street_number":"2","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@baronian.eu","website":"http:\/\/www.baronian.eu","phone_contact":"+32 2 512 92 95","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue Isidore Verheyden, 2","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":"Albert Baronian est l\u2019un des galeristes les plus embl\u00e9matiques de la capitale. Il a d\u00e9but\u00e9 ses activit\u00e9s dans les ann\u00e9es 70. La programmation de sa galerie refl\u00e8te ses gouts \u00e9clectiques et sensibles. Les artistes du mouvement de l\u2019arte povera comme Alighiero e Boetti ou Mario Merz y trouvent une vitrine belge pour valoriser leur travail. Gilbert & Georges, Tony Oursler, Bruno Serralongue, Robert Devriendt\u2026 Le programme de la galerie est consacr\u00e9 \u00e0 l\u2019art contemporain ainsi qu'aux mouvements artistiques et aux artistes importants qui ont marqu\u00e9 les quarante derni\u00e8res ann\u00e9es. Toute proche de la place St\u00e9phanie, la galerie compte deux espaces distincts mais se faisant quasiment face : la galerie principale est install\u00e9e dans la rue Isidore Verheyden et l\u2019annexe \u00e0 la rue de la Concorde. ","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":"Baronian ","virtual_visit":null},"nl":{"name":"Baronian","address_street_name":"Isidore Verheydenstraat","address_street_number":"2","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@baronian.eu","website":"http:\/\/www.baronian.eu","phone_contact":"+32 2 512 92 95","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Elsene","address_line1":"Isidore Verheydenstraat, 2","address_line2":"1050 Elsene","description_web":"Albert Baronian is een van de meest emblematische galerijhouders in de hoofdstad, met een carri\u00e8re die eind jaren 1970 begon. Het programma van zijn galerij weerspiegelt zijn eclectische en gevoelige smaak. Kunstenaars van de arte-poverabeweging zoals Alighiero e Boetti of Mario Merz vinden er een Belgische vitrine voor hun werk. Nu circuleren er namen als Gilbert & Georges, Tony Oursler, Bruno Serralongue, Robert Devriendt en vele anderen. Het programma van de galerij is daarmee zowel gewijd aan de hedendaagse kunst als aan de kunststromingen en kunstenaars die de laatste veertig jaar hun stempel hebben gedrukt. Vlakbij het Stefaniaplein beschikt de galerie over twee verschillende, maar bijna tegenover elkaar liggende ruimtes: de hoofdgalerie bevindt zich in de Isidore Verheydenstraat en het bijgebouw in de Eendrachtsstraat. ","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":"Baronian ","virtual_visit":null},"en":{"name":"Baronian","address_street_name":"Rue Isidore Verheyden","address_street_number":"2","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@baronian.eu","website":"http:\/\/www.baronian.eu","phone_contact":"+32 2 512 92 95","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue Isidore Verheyden, 2","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":"Albert Baronian is one of the most emblematic gallery owners in the capital and began his activities in the 1970s. The programme of his gallery reflects his eclectic and sensitive tastes. Artists from the arte povera movement such as Alighiero e Boetti or Mario Merz are given a Belgian showcase for their work. Gilbert & Georges, Tony Oursler, Bruno Serralongue, Robert Devriendt... The gallery's programme is devoted to contemporary art as well as to important artistic movements and artists who have marked the last forty years. Close to place St\u00e9phanie, the gallery has two distinct, but almost opposite spaces: the main gallery is located in rue Isidore Verheyden and the annex in rue de la Concorde.  \r\nAlbert Baronian opened his first gallery in 1973 and immediately enjoyed international success thanks to the presentation of Arte Povera artists Alighiero e Boetti, Mario Merz, Giulio Paolini, Gilberto Zorio. Later, as the president of the Galleries\u2019 Association, the Brussels Art fair took a more international turn whilst under his direction. He sees the responsibility of the gallery as three folds: to work for the long term development of each artists\u2019 career, acting as a liaison to international galleries and museums as well as placing works in collections; to create an historical archive for each artist; and to act as an accessible public space in which the exhibitions become an exemplary gesture of the power of subjectivity to the audience at large. The program is dedicated to contemporary art as well as important artistic movements and artists that have defined the last forty years. \u00bb \r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":"Baronian ","virtual_visit":null},"de":{"name":"Baronian Xippas","address_street_name":"Rue Isidore Verheyden","address_street_number":"2","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@baronian.eu","website":"http:\/\/www.baronian.eu","phone_contact":"+32 2 512 92 95","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue Isidore Verheyden, 2","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"it":{"name":"Baronian Xippas","address_street_name":"Rue Isidore Verheyden","address_street_number":"2","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@baronian.eu","website":"http:\/\/www.baronian.eu","phone_contact":"+32 2 512 92 95","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue Isidore Verheyden, 2","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"sp":{"name":"Baronian Xippas","address_street_name":"Rue Isidore Verheyden","address_street_number":"2","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@baronian.eu","website":"http:\/\/www.baronian.eu","phone_contact":"+32 2 512 92 95","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue Isidore Verheyden, 2","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"pt":{"name":"Baronian Xippas","address_street_name":"Rue Isidore Verheyden","address_street_number":"2","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@baronian.eu","website":"http:\/\/www.baronian.eu","phone_contact":"+32 2 512 92 95","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue Isidore Verheyden, 2","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","desc