eert ons door de spontane creaties. Ze ontstaan doelbewust of ongewild, die magische en authentieke fragmenten van de intimiteit van onbekenden die meer dan een eeuw geleden leefden. Een knipoog naar de ijdelheid van het kortstondige, welwillende geesten die lang beschermd waren in de schaduw van vergeten albums. Ze verrassen ons met hun nabijheid, intieme albums die weerloos opengerukt eindigden op de rommelmarkt, stille getuigen van een tijd waarin fotografie niet als gevaarlijk werd beschouwd. ","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"en":{"name":"TinyGallery Brussels","address_street_name":"Rue de la Cuve","address_street_number":"26","address_street_box":null,"email":"ogc@ogc.be","website":"http:\/\/www.tinygallery.photo","phone_contact":"+32 475 27 95 56","phone_booking":"+32 472 27 95 56","address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue de la Cuve, 26","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":"TinyGallery - Small museum of amateur photography - wishes to preserve amateur photography and pay tribute to the anonymous artists who authored them.\r\n\r\nWhether produced intentionally or accidentally, amateur photography fascinates us with its spontaneous creations. Magical, raw moments are captured, allowing us an intimate insight into the lives of strangers who lived over a century ago. In a nod to the vanity of the ephemeral, these benevolent ghosts, who have long been protected by the shadows of the past, surprise us with their proximity. Battered and bruised albums scattered over flea markets surrender to us defencelessly, bearing witness to a time when photography was not considered dangerous. ","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"de":{"name":"TinyGallery Brussels","address_street_name":"Rue de la Cuve","address_street_number":"26","address_street_box":null,"email":"ogc@ogc.be","website":"http:\/\/www.tinygallery.photo","phone_contact":"+32 475 