":{}},"visit_profile":{"list":[337],"translations":{"fr":["Highlight"],"nl":["Highlight"],"en":["Highlight"],"de":["Highlight"],"it":["Highlight"],"sp":["Highlight"],"pt":[null],"cn":[null]}},"tags":[],"accessibilities":{"list":[255,263],"translations":{"fr":["Accessible","Accessible aux pi\u00e9tons appareill\u00e9s"],"nl":["Toegankelijk","Toegankelijk voor voetgangers met hulpmiddelen"],"en":["Accessible","Accessible to pedestrians with mobility aids"],"de":["Barrierefrei","Barrierefrei f\u00fcr Fu\u00dfg\u00e4nger mit Gehhilfe"],"it":["Accessibile","Accessibile ai pedoni con supporti"],"sp":["Habilitado","Habilitado para peatones con aud\u00edfonos"],"pt":[null,null],"cn":[null,null]}},"facebook_link":null,"publication_state":"public","last_updated_at":"2023-02-13T03:05:24+01:00","published_at":"2022-09-05T13:26:32+02:00","backoffice_id":261022,"import_origin":null,"sub_type":"expo","show_in_agenda":true,"ranking":0.28599248869989},{"id":550164,"date_start":"2023-02-01","date_end":"2023-05-01","date_next":"2023-02-14","accept_article27":false,"accept_cultuurbon":false,"accept_paspartoe":false,"is_closed_on_public_holidays":false,"is_closed_on_school_holidays":false,"is_only_by_appointment":false,"is_permanent":false,"is_free":false,"is_online":false,"is_canceled":false,"is_soldout":false,"categories":{"main":{"id":23,"translations":{"fr":"Exposition","nl":"Tentoonstellingen","en":"Exhibition","de":"Ausstellung","it":"Esposizioni","sp":"Exhibici\u00f3n","pt":null,"cn":null}},"others":{"list":[24,27],"translations":{"fr":["Galeries d'art","Photographie"],"nl":["Galeries","Fotografie"],"en":["Art Galleries","Photography"],"de":["Kunstgalerien","Fotografie"],"it":["Gallerie d'arte","Fotografia"],"sp":["Galer\u00edas de arte","Fotograf\u00eda"],"pt":[null,null],"cn":[null,null]}}},"languages":{"spoken":["fr","nl","en"],"subtitles":[]},"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Iran","shortdescr":"Au vu de la r\u00e9volte qui se d\u00e9roule actuellement en Iran, nous accueillerons cinq photographes pour d\u00e9peindre l\u2019histoire de l\u2019Iran.","longdescr":"Cette exposition sera form\u00e9e en deux volets, le premier qui reviendra sur les cinquante derni\u00e8res ann\u00e9es, puis le second volet mettra en valeur la r\u00e9volte actuelle. Par ailleurs, une fresque compos\u00e9e des actualit\u00e9s trouv\u00e9es sur les r\u00e9seaux sociaux mettra en valeur l\u2019impossibilit\u00e9 des journalistes \u00e0 se rendre sur place pour faire leur travail.\r\nEn parall\u00e8le se d\u00e9rouleront des \u00e9v\u00e9nements et des performances avec des artistes et des personnes issues de la communaut\u00e9 iranienne pr\u00e9sentes en Belgique.\r\n\r\nLe premier photographe pr\u00e9sent\u00e9 est Eric Bouvet, un fran\u00e7ais qui, depuis les ann\u00e9es 90, couvre les conflits en Afghanistan, Irak, Iran, Tch\u00e9tch\u00e9nie, Soudan, Somalie, ex-Yougoslavie, Liban, Isra\u00ebl. Irlande du Nord, Kurdistan, Surinam, Burundi, Libye et Ukraine. Son travail a \u00e9t\u00e9 publi\u00e9 dans de nombreux magazines internationaux comme le Time, Life, Newsweek, Paris-Match, etc. Au cours de sa carri\u00e8re, il a \u00e9t\u00e9 r\u00e9compens\u00e9 par diff\u00e9rents prix : Prix Paris-Match (1986), World Press (1986), Laur\u00e9at du prix de la fondation W. Eugene Smith (1997), Laur\u00e9at de la fondation 3P (2004).\r\n\r\nLe second photojournaliste, Alain Keler, a couvert des conflits comme ceux en Isra\u00ebl, le mouvement Solidarno\u015b\u0107 en Pologne, en Irlande du Nord, la r\u00e9volte des \u00e9tudiants de la place Tian\u2019anmen \u00e0 P\u00e9kin, la famine en \u00c9thiopie, les guerres au Liban, au Salvador ou en Tch\u00e9tch\u00e9nie. Il a \u00e9t\u00e9 r\u00e9compens\u00e9 par son travail \u00e0 travers l\u2019obtention de 5 World Press Awards, 2 Visa d'Or, la m\u00e9daille d'or du 15e anniversaire de la photographie, prix Bayeux-Calvados, un Front Line Club Award, ainsi qu'un Paris-Match Award.\r\n\r\nEnsuite, Michel Setboun, photographe d'origine alg\u00e9rienne, sera \u00e9galement pr\u00e9sent\u00e9. Au cours de sa carri\u00e8re pour l'agence Sipa, il a remport\u00e9 en 1984, le premier prix du World Press Photo.\r\n\r\nLe quatri\u00e8me porte le nom de Reza, de son nom complet Reza Deghati. C'est un photojournaliste fran\u00e7ais d'origine az\u00e9rie d'Iran qui a travaill\u00e9 dans le monde entier, notamment pour National Geographic. Son travail est pr\u00e9sent\u00e9 dans les m\u00e9dias internationaux (National Geographic, Time Magazine, Stern, Newsweek, El Pa\u00eds, Paris Match, Geo...), ainsi que dans une s\u00e9rie de livres, d'expositions et de documentaires r\u00e9alis\u00e9s pour la National Geographic Channel. Son travail a \u00e9t\u00e9 r\u00e9compens\u00e9 par le World Press Photo, l'Infinity Award, le Lucy Award, une m\u00e9daille honorifique de l'Universit\u00e9 du Missouri et le titre honorifique de Docteur Honoris Causa de l'Universit\u00e9 am\u00e9ricaine de Paris. La France l'a \u00e9galement nomm\u00e9 Chevalier de l'Ordre national du M\u00e9rite.\r\n\r\nPour cette exposition, nous accueillerons aussi Marie Tihon, journaliste ind\u00e9pendante belge. Membre de Women Photograph, elle documente principalement la lutte pour les droits des femmes. \u00c0 travers ses reportages, elle se concentre sur la r\u00e9silience, les luttes pour la justice et la migration. Elle a remport\u00e9 le prix du jury et le prix du public du Mentor Award en 2016 au festival Visa Pour l'Image de Perpignan. En 2018, elle a \u00e9t\u00e9 s\u00e9lectionn\u00e9e pour participer \u00e0 l'Acad\u00e9mie Nikon-Noor et elle a remport\u00e9 la bourse Vocatio. Son travail a \u00e9t\u00e9 publi\u00e9 dans le Courrier International, Lib\u00e9ration, Le Figaro Magazine, The Atlantic, Al Jazeera, Stern, Vice, etc.\r\n\r\nPour finir, nous rendrons hommage au travail d'Abbas, photojournaliste d\u00e9c\u00e9d\u00e9 en 2018. Durant sa carri\u00e8re, il s'est consacr\u00e9 \u00e0 la documentation de la vie politique et sociale des soci\u00e9t\u00e9s en conflit. Dans son \u0153uvre majeure depuis 1970, il a couvert les guerres et les r\u00e9volutions au Biafra, au Bangladesh, en Irlande du Nord, au Vietnam, au Moyen-Orient, au Chili, \u00e0 Cuba et en Afrique du Sud pendant l'apartheid.","performers":"Eric Bouvet, Alain Keler, Michel Setboun, Reza Deghati, Marie Tihon, Abbas","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/geopolis.brussels","email":"contact@geopolis.brussels","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/fr\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.550164"},"nl":{"name":"Iran","shortdescr":"In het licht van de aanhoudende opstand in Iran verwelkomen we vijf fotografen om de geschiedenis van Iran in beeld te brengen.","longdescr":"De tentoonstelling bestaat uit twee delen, waarvan het eerste deel terugblikt op de afgelopen vijftig jaar en het tweede deel de huidige opstand belicht. Bovendien zal een muurschildering van op sociale netwerken gevonden nieuws de onmogelijkheid voor journalisten belichten om daar hun werk te doen.\r\nDaarnaast zijn er evenementen en optredens met kunstenaars en mensen uit de Iraanse gemeenschap in Belgi\u00eb.\r\n\r\nDe eerste fotograaf die wordt voorgesteld is Eric Bouvet, een Fransman die sinds de jaren negentig conflicten in Afghanistan, Irak, Iran, Tsjetsjeni\u00eb, Soedan, Somali\u00eb, ex-Joegoslavi\u00eb, Libanon en Isra\u00ebl verslaat. Noord-Ierland, Koerdistan, Suriname, Burundi, Libi\u00eb en Oekra\u00efne. Zijn werk is gepubliceerd in talrijke internationale tijdschriften zoals Time, Life, Newsweek, Paris-Match, enz. Tijdens zijn carri\u00e8re heeft hij verschillende prijzen gewonnen: Paris-Match Prize (1986), World Press (1986), W. Eugene Smith Foundation Award (1997), 3P Foundation Award (2004).\r\n\r\nDe tweede fotojournalist, Alain Keler, heeft verslag gedaan van conflicten zoals die in Isra\u00ebl, de Solidarno\u015b\u0107-beweging in Polen, Noord-Ierland, de studentenopstand op het Tian'anmen-plein in Peking, de hongersnood in Ethiopi\u00eb, de oorlogen in Libanon, El Salvador of Tsjetsjeni\u00eb. Zijn werk werd bekroond met 5 World Press Awards, 2 Visa d'Or, de gouden medaille van de 15e verjaardag van de fotografie, de prijs Bayeux-Calvados, een Front Line Club Award en een Paris-Match Award.\r\n\r\nVervolgens wordt Michel Setboun, een fotograaf van Algerijnse afkomst, voorgesteld. Tijdens zijn carri\u00e8re bij het agentschap Sipa won hij in 1984 de eerste World Press Photo award.\r\n\r\nDe vierde is Reza, die voluit Reza Deghati heet. Hij is een Franse fotojournalist van Azerische afkomst uit Iran die over de hele wereld heeft gewerkt, met name voor National Geographic. Zijn werk was te zien in internationale media (National Geographic, Time Magazine, Stern, Newsweek, El Pa\u00eds, Paris Match, Geo...) en in een reeks boeken, tentoonstellingen en documentaires voor National Geographic Channel. Zijn werk is bekroond met de World Press Photo, de Infinity Award, de Lucy Award, een erepenning van de Universiteit van Missouri en de eretitel Doctor Honoris Causa van de Amerikaanse Universiteit in Parijs. Frankrijk heeft hem ook benoemd tot Chevalier de l'Ordre national du M\u00e9rite.\r\n\r\nVoor deze tentoonstelling verwelkomen we ook Marie Tihon, een Belgische freelance journaliste. Als lid van Women Photograph documenteert ze vooral de strijd voor vrouwenrechten. Met haar verslaggeving richt ze zich op veerkracht, strijd voor rechtvaardigheid en migratie. Ze won de Mentor Award Jury Prize en de Publieksprijs in 2016 op het Visa Pour l'Image festival in Perpignan. In 2018 werd ze geselecteerd om deel te nemen aan de Nikon-Noor Academy en won ze de Vocatio beurs. Haar werk is gepubliceerd in Courrier International, Lib\u00e9ration, Le Figaro Magazine, The Atlantic, Al Jazeera, Stern, Vice, enz.\r\n\r\nTot slot brengen we een eerbetoon aan het werk van Abbas, een fotojournalist die in 2018 is overleden. Tijdens zijn carri\u00e8re wijdde hij zich aan het documenteren van het politieke en sociale leven van samenlevingen in conflict. In zijn belangrijkste werk sinds 1970 versloeg hij oorlogen en revoluties in Biafra, Bangladesh, Noord-Ierland, Vietnam, het Midden-Oosten, Chili, Cuba en Zuid-Afrika tijdens de apartheid.","performers":"Eric Bouvet, Alain Keler, Michel Setboun, Reza Deghati, Marie Tihon, Abbas","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/geopolis.brussels","email":"contact@geopolis.brussels","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/nl\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.550164"},"en":{"name":"Iran","shortdescr":"In light of the ongoing uprising in Iran, we will welcome five photographers to depict the history of Iran.","longdescr":"This exhibition will be formed in two parts, the first one will look back at the last fifty years, then the second part will highlight the current revolt. In addition, a mural composed of news found on social networks will highlight the impossibility of journalists to go there to do their work.\r\nIn parallel, events and performances with artists and people from the Iranian community in Belgium will take place.\r\n\r\nThe first photographer presented is Eric Bouvet, a Frenchman who, since the 90s, has been covering conflicts in Afghanistan, Iraq, Iran, Chechnya, Sudan, Somalia, ex-Yugoslavia, Lebanon, Israel. Northern Ireland, Kurdistan, Surinam, Burundi, Libya and Ukraine. His work has been published in many international magazines such as Time, Life, Newsweek, Paris-Match, etc. During his career, he has been awarded various prizes: Paris-Match Prize (1986), World Press (1986), W. Eugene Smith Foundation Award (1997), 3P Foundation Award (2004).\r\n\r\nThe second photojournalist, Alain Keler, has covered conflicts such as those in Israel, the Solidarno\u015b\u0107 movement in Poland, Northern Ireland, the student revolt in Tian'anmen Square in Beijing, the famine in Ethiopia, the wars in Lebanon, El Salvador or Chechnya. His work has been rewarded with 5 World Press Awards, 2 Visa d'Or, the Gold Medal of the 15th Anniversary of Photography, Bayeux-Calvados Award, a Front Line Club Award, and a Paris-Match Award.\r\n\r\nThen, Michel Setboun, photographer of Algerian origin, will also be presented. During his career for the Sipa agency, he won the first World Press Photo award in 1984.\r\n\r\nThe fourth is named Reza, from his full name Reza Deghati. He is a French photojournalist of Azeri origin from Iran who has worked all over the world, notably for National Geographic. His work has been featured in international media (National Geographic, Time Magazine, Stern, Newsweek, El Pa\u00eds, Paris Match, Geo...), as well as in a series of books, exhibitions and documentaries made for the National Geographic Channel. His work has been awarded the World Press Photo, the Infinity Award, the Lucy Award, an honorary medal from the University of Missouri and the honorary title of Doctor Honoris Causa from the American University of Paris. France has also named him a Chevalier de l'Ordre national du M\u00e9rite.\r\n\r\nFor this exhibition, we will also welcome Marie Tihon, a Belgian freelance journalist. Member of Women Photograph, she mainly documents the struggle for women's rights. Through her reporting, she focuses on resilience, struggles for justice and migration. She won the Mentor Award Jury Prize and Audience Prize in 2016 at the Visa Pour l'Image festival in Perpignan. In 2018, she was selected to participate in the Nikon-Noor Academy and won the Vocatio Fellowship. Her work has been published in Courrier International, Lib\u00e9ration, Le Figaro Magazine, The Atlantic, Al Jazeera, Stern, Vice, etc.\r\n\r\nFinally, we will pay tribute to the work of Abbas, a photojournalist who passed away in 2018. During his career, he dedicated himself to documenting the political and social life of societies in conflict. In his major work since 1970, he covered wars and revolutions in Biafra, Bangladesh, Northern Ireland, Vietnam, the Middle East, Chile, Cuba and South Africa during apartheid.","performers":"Eric Bouvet, Alain Keler, Michel Setboun, Reza Deghati, Marie Tihon, Abbas","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/geopolis.brussels","email":"contact@geopolis.brussels","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/en\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.550164"},"de":{"name":"Iran","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/geopolis.brussels","email":"contact@geopolis.brussels","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/de\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.550164"},"it":{"name":"Iran","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/geopolis.brussels","email":"contact@geopolis.brussels","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/it\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.550164"},"sp":{"name":"Iran","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/geopolis.brussels","email":"contact@geopolis.brussels","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/sp\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.550164"},"pt":{"name":"Iran","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/geopolis.brussels","email":"contact@geopolis.brussels","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/pt\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.550164"},"cn":{"name":"Iran","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/geopolis.brussels","email":"contact@geopolis.brussels","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/cn\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.550164"}},"place":{"id":269816,"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Geopolis","address_street_name":"Rue des Tanneurs","address_street_number":"58-60","address_street_box":null,"email":"contact@geopolis.brussels","website":"http:\/\/geopolis.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 485 32 85 90","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue des Tanneurs, 58-60","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"G\u00e9opolis est parrain\u00e9 par le photoreporter de guerre Laurent Van der Stockt, et port\u00e9 par trois militants associatifs, passionn\u00e9s de g\u00e9opolitique. Cet espace culturel d\u00e9di\u00e9 au photo-reportage d\u2019actualit\u00e9 et d\u2019histoire est install\u00e9 au c\u0153ur de Bruxelles (aux Ateliers des Tanneurs) et propose des cycles d\u2019expositions th\u00e9matiques et une programmation \u00e9v\u00e9nementielle tourn\u00e9e vers le grand public et notamment les jeunes.  \r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"nl":{"name":"Geopolis","address_street_name":"Huidevettersstraat","address_street_number":"58-60","address_street_box":null,"email":"contact@geopolis.brussels","website":"http:\/\/geopolis.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 485 32 85 90","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussel","address_line1":"Huidevettersstraat, 58-60","address_line2":"1000 Brussel","description_web":"G\u00e9opolis is een centrum voor fotojournalistiek en onderwijs opgericht in 2017 door een klein team met een passie voor geopolitiek. Door fototentoonstellingen en didactische tentoonstellingen te combineren met evenementen en een radioprogramma, beoogt ze actuele vraagstukken bespreekbaar te maken. Het centrum, gevestigd in de Ateliers des Tanneurs op een bijzondere en polyvalente locatie, organiseert tentoonstellingen over actuele en geschiedkundige thema\u2019s met werk van zowel gevestigde fotografen als jonge talenten.","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"en":{"name":"Geopolis","address_street_name":"Rue des Tanneurs","address_street_number":"58-60","address_s